{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Sewdeg696sTVzKczVotosZ","type":"tool_result","content":"28:## Experiment presentation (reproduce VERBATIM — identical across all experiments)\n29-\n30-The implemented jsPsych experiment must be identical in every experiment and every\n31-run; **only the stimuli change.** Use the wording below exactly (do not\n32-paraphrase), **button responses only**, and the data contract above (`chose_left`,\n33-`sequence_a`, `sequence_b`).\n34-\n35-> **Rendering note (the wording below is Markdown — convert it to HTML).** The\n36-> `**bold**` spans must render as `<strong>` in the experiment; participants must\n37-> never see literal asterisks. Put each paragraph in its own `<p>`, and wrap the\n38-> instructions and debrief in the skeleton's `<div class=\"auto-psych-prose\">`\n39-> (constrained-width, left-aligned) so the text does not span the full screen.\n40-\n41-- **Instructions** (first screen, button labelled `Begin`) — use this wording exactly:\n42-  > In this study, you will look at sequences of coin flips and judge how\n43-  > **random** they look.\n44-  >\n45-  > Imagine flipping a fair coin over and over. Each flip is equally likely to come\n46-  > up Heads (H) or Tails (T), and every flip is independent — the coin has no\n47-  > memory, so what came before does not change what comes next.\n48-  >\n49-  > On each trial you will see **two** sequences of coin flips, side by side. The\n50-  > two sequences will have the **same length**. Your task is to pick the **one\n51-  > sequence that looks more random** to you — the one that looks more like it was\n52-  > produced by genuinely random coin flipping.\n53-  >\n54-  > Different people have different impressions of what makes a sequence look\n55-  > random, and there are no right or wrong answers. We are interested in your own\n56-  > honest impression, so go with your gut. You will complete **64 trials**, which\n57-  > takes about 7 minutes. Your responses are anonymous.\n58-\n59-  > **Wording rationale (not shown to participants).** This instruction is grounded\n60-  > in the subjective-randomness literature, which warns that naming the structural\n61-  > cues under study (run length / \"streakiness\", alternation / \"switching\", H–T\n62-  > balance) coaches participants and confounds the measurement (Nickerson, 2002,\n63-  > *Psychol. Rev.*; Reimers, Donkin & Le Pelley, 2018, *Cognition*). The accepted\n64-  > practice is to define the generating process — a *fair coin*, 50/50,\n65-  > independent flips — but leave the meaning of \"random-looking\" for the\n66-  > participant to supply from their own intuition (Williams & Griffiths, 2013,\n67-  > *JEP:General*, Exp. 3 nested condition; Griffiths, Daniels, Austerweil &\n68-  > Tenenbaum, 2018, *Cognitive Psychology*). The question phrasing \"which … looks\n----\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>Experiment</title>\n    <script src=\"https://unpkg.com/jspsych@7.3.4\"></script>\n    <link\n      href=\"https://unpkg.com/jspsych@7.3.4/css/jspsych.css\"\n      rel=\"stylesheet\"\n    />\n    <script src=\"https://unpkg.com/@jspsych/plugin-html-button-response@1.1.3\"></script>\n    <style>\n      /* Readable prose block for instructions/debrief — constrained width, left\n       aligned, comfortable line height. Without this, text spans the full screen. */\n      .auto-psych-prose {\n        max-width: 620px;\n        margin: 0 auto;\n        text-align: left;\n        line-height: 1.6;\n        font-size: 18px;\n      }\n      .auto-psych-prose p {\n        margin: 0 0 1em;\n      }\n      .auto-psych-pair {\n        display: flex;\n        justify-content: center;\n        gap: 64px;\n        margin: 24px 0;\n      }\n      .auto-psych-seq {\n        font-family: monospace;\n        font-size: 28px;\n        letter-spacing: 4px;\n      }\n      .jspsych-btn {\n        padding: 12px 28px;\n        font-size: 18px;\n        border-radius: 8px;\n      }\n    </style>\n  </head>\n  <body></body>\n  <script>\n  {\n    \"sequence_a\": \"HTTHHTTH\",\n    \"sequence_b\": \"THTHTHHH\",\n    \"eig\": 0.354893,\n    \"selection_rank\": 1,\n    \"joint_eig_bits\": 1.118734,\n    \"source\": \"eig\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"sequence_a\": \"HTHHHHHT\",\n    \"sequence_b\": \"HTHTTHTH\",\n    \"eig\": 0.242014,\n    \"selection_rank\": 2,\n    \"joint_eig_bits\": 1.654361,\n    \"source\": \"eig\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"sequence_a\": \"HTHTHTHT\",\n    \"sequence_b\": \"HTTTTTTT\",\n    \"eig\": 0.149617,\n    \"selection_rank\": 3,\n    \"joint_eig_bits\": 1.862099,\n    \"source\": \"eig\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"sequence_a\": \"HHHHTTTT\",\n    \"sequence_b\": \"HTHHTHHT\",\n    \"eig\": 0.271807,\n    \"selection_rank\": 4,\n    \"joint_eig_bits\": 1.925998,\n    \"source\": \"eig\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"sequence_a\": \"HHTTHHT\",\n    \"sequence_b\": \"TTTTTTH\",\n    \"eig\": 0.159836,\n    \"selection_rank\": 5,\n    \"joint_eig_bits\": 1.947151,\n    \"source\": \"eig\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"sequence_a\": \"HHHHHHHT\",\n    \"sequence_b\": \"TTTTTTTT\",\n    \"eig\": 0.062207,\n    \"selection_rank\": 6,\n    \"joint_eig_bits\": 1.959171,\n    \"source\": \"eig\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"sequence_a\": \"HTTTHHT\",\n    \"sequence_b\": \"TTTTTTH\",\n    \"eig\": 0.277473,\n    \"selection_rank\": 7,\n    \"joint_eig_bits\": 1.963196,\n    \"source\": \"eig\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"sequence_a\": \"HHHHHHHT\",\n    \"sequence_b\": \"HTHTHTHT\",\n    \"eig\": 0.135983,\n    \"selection_rank\": 8,\n    \"joint_eig_bits\": 1.970633,\n    \"source\": \"eig\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"sequence_a\": \"HHHHHHHH\",\n    \"sequence_b\": \"HHHHHHHT\",\n    \"eig\": 0.073794,\n    \"selection_rank\": 9,\n    \"joint_eig_bits\": 1.976269,\n    \"source\": \"eig\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"sequence_a\": \"HTHTTHTH\",\n    \"sequence_b\": \"HTTHTTHT\",\n    \"e